{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEach prompt-eval spec in `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` pins the model it generates with in a top-level `model:` key (for example `plan-review-finder.eval.yaml:11` is `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`; `plan-review-evidence-kind.eval.yaml:5` is `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`), read by `rebar.llm.evals.eval` at `eval.py:308` (`gen_model = spec.get(\"model\")`). After the configured models move to the 5.5 generation (sibling task `beaten-natural-grouse`), these pins would keep the prompt evals measuring the retired models, so the evals could not show whether the prompts still pass on the models that actually run.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove every spec pin to the 5.5 id of the same family and provider, keeping the provider each spec names: `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` to `anthropic:claude-opus-5-5`, `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` to `anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5`, `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` to `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, and any Haiku pin to `claude-haiku-5-5`. Run the prompt evals the `eval-live` job defines (`.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml`: `rebar.llm.evals.eval.run_eval` over each dataset-bearing spec at `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12`) once on the 4.x pins before the change and once on the 5.5 pins after, with `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`, and record both summaries (spec, pass/fail, coverage) as a ticket comment. The commit is stacked on the upgrade task's commit (Gerrit parent), so it cannot land first, and the after-run is made on that stack because the 5.5 request-surface fixes (no temperature, explicit effort, corrected profile) must be in place for it to be meaningful; a one-to-one family mapping keeps each spec measuring the same tier it was calibrated on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml (the `model:` line of each spec that pins a 4.x model; no other line changes)\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/unit` eval-discipline checks (the offline tier `_eval-discipline.yml` runs) pass, so spec validation still accepts every edited file.\n- Live: the before and after prompt-eval runs described above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` prints nothing.\n- [x] The before (4.x) and after (5.5) prompt-eval summaries are recorded in a ticket comment, one line per spec with pass/fail and coverage.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794372285593989454,"uuid":"116de4c0-8318-47be-a023-ea875f0ea720"}